       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Sertraline 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Higher doses raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and they haven't been shown to work better. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Enter 200 mg PO once daily**, the maximum labeled dose.\n2. **Enter a different dose**, such as 50 mg or 100 mg daily. 50 mg is the usual starting dose for depression, and 25 mg is the usual starting dose for panic disorder or PTSD.\n3. **Enter 400 mg as written.** This would be intentional off-label dosing. Please confirm that, and I can add a note to the order such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max; confirmed by attending.\" Pharmacy may still ask you to verify it.\n\nTell me which one, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
